    "q-138807": {
      "dom_id": "step-q138807",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "Consider the function $y=(3{x}^{2})^{x}.$ Its derivative is given by \n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=(3{x}^{2})^{x}\\cdot g(x).\n$$\n\nFind the function $g(x).$",
      "worked_solution": "We have the function \n\n$$\ny=(3{x}^{2})^{x}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we take the natural logarithm of both sides:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡y & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡((3{x}^{2})^{x}) \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡y & =x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3{x}^{2})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we differentiate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡y) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3{x}^{2})) \\\\ \\frac{1}{y}\\cdot {y}^{′} & =(x)^{′}\\cdot (\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3{x}^{2}))+(x)\\cdot {(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3{x}^{2}))}^{′} \\\\ \\frac{1}{y}\\cdot {y}^{′} & =1\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}⁡(3{x}^{2})+x\\cdot (\\frac{1}{3{x}^{2}}\\cdot 6x) \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{′}}{y} & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3{x}^{2})+2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve for ${y}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =y(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3{x}^{2})+2)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute $y=(3{x}^{2})^{x}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =(3{x}^{2})^{x}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3{x}^{2})+2)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $g(x)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3{x}^{2})+2.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-138807-a",
